Guest fio, both block paths, re-run after delta packs and concurrent uploads.

host:     AWS i4i.metal, real KVM, Cloud Hypervisor, real in-region S3
build:    this branch; fio in the golden image, 4 vCPU / 2 GiB Cat, ext4 root,
          --direct=1, 1 GiB file, 10 s runtime, 2 s ramp, single sample per point
date_utc: 2026-07-27

Why re-run: ADR-0015 keeps `kernel-nbd` as the default and names its flip
criterion (a) "delta pack lands and brings commit cost down". It did. But the
comparison behind "buffered NBD wins on writes" was taken on a flush-bound engine
that wrote ~200 MiB per commit, and that premise is gone, so the comparison had to
be taken again.

Configuration is as deployed: the node agent opens /dev/nbdN with direct=off, so
the kernel-nbd rows have the host page cache in front of them and the vhost-user
rows do not.

